Merge Sort Algorithm (Pseudocode):

MergeSort(A, p, r)
if p < r
    q = floor((p + r) / 2)
    MergeSort(A, p, q)
    MergeSort(A, q + 1, r)
    Merge(A, p, q, r)

Sorting Sequence: {23, 11, 5, 15, 68, 31, 4, 17}

Step-by-step Execution:
1. Divide the array into individual single-element lists:
   - {23, 11, 5, 15} and {68, 31, 4, 17}
   - Further divide: {23, 11}, {5, 15}, {68, 31}, {4, 17}
   - Single elements: {23}, {11}, {5}, {15}, {68}, {31}, {4}, {17}

2. Merge step-by-step (combining and sorting):
   - Merge {23} and {11} -> {11, 23}
   - Merge {5} and {15} -> {5, 15}
   - Merge {68} and {31} -> {31, 68}
   - Merge {4} and {17} -> {4, 17}

3. Merge pairs of sorted sublists:
   - Merge {11, 23} and {5, 15} -> {5, 11, 15, 23}
   - Merge {31, 68} and {4, 17} -> {4, 17, 31, 68}

4. Final Merge:
   - Merge {5, 11, 15, 23} and {4, 17, 31, 68} -> {4, 5, 11, 15, 17, 23, 31, 68}

Final Sorted Array: {4, 5, 11, 15, 17, 23, 31, 68}.
